# 🧭 RULE.md Template — Decision Tree

Use **Template A** (Principle-based) for single, focused principles with Why/How structure (e.g., guiding_principles.md).
Use **Template B** (Constraint/Pattern-based) for multiple related patterns with emoji headers and callout blocks (e.g., behaviour.md, security.md).

## 📋 Contents

- [Template A — Single Principle](#-template-a--single-principle)
- [Template B — Constraint/Pattern-Based](#-template-b--constraintpattern-based)
- [Quality Checklist — Both Templates](#-quality-checklist--both-templates)

---

## 📋 Template A — Single Principle

Use when: one core concept, Why/How structure, ~50-60 lines.

```markdown
# 🔄 [Principle Name]

**Purpose:** One-line statement of what this principle establishes.

[Opening paragraph: context, why it matters, who it applies to.]

---

## 📐 The Rule

[The core principle, 1–3 sentences, clear and actionable.]

---

## **Why**

[Rationale: the underlying problem, historical context, or constraint that makes this rule necessary.]

---

## **How to apply**

[Guidance on when and how to follow the rule. Concrete examples welcome.]

---

## Related

Link to related principles or rules via `[[memory-slug]]` or `@~/.claude/_rules/<path>`.
```

**Characteristics:**
- Purpose statement (one line)
- H1 emoji header
- 50–70 lines
- Bold **Why:** and **How to apply:** sections
- Trailing newline

---

## 📋 Template B — Constraint/Pattern-Based

Use when: multiple related patterns, enforcement-style, ~80-110 lines.

```markdown
# 🛡️ [Domain] Rules

**Purpose:** One-line statement of what these rules establish.

Rules governing [domain/concern].

## 🔬 [Pattern 1 Name]

- **[Bullet 1]:** one-line explanation.
  - **Note:** caveat or edge case (optional).
- **[Bullet 2]:** one-line explanation.
  - **Example:** concrete illustration (optional).

---

## ⚙️ [Pattern 2 Name]

- **[Bullet 1]:** one-line explanation.
- **[Bullet 2]:** one-line explanation.

---

## 🚨 [Pattern 3 Name] — Edge Cases

| Scenario | Guidance |
|----------|----------|
| **[Case 1]** | [What to do and why] |
| **[Case 2]** | [What to do and why] |

---

## Related

Link to related rules or guidance.
```

**Characteristics:**
- Purpose statement (one line)
- H1 emoji header
- Section emoji headers (`##`)
- Bold keywords in bullets (`**Why:**`, `**Note:**`, `**Example:**`)
- One sentence per bullet
- 80–110 lines
- Trailing newline

---

## ✅ Quality Checklist — Both Templates

- [ ] **Purpose present:** One-line statement at top
- [ ] **H1 emoji header:** File title with emoji
- [ ] **H2 section headers:** All start with emoji (scannability)
- [ ] **Bold keywords:** Bullets open with `**term:**`
- [ ] **One sentence per bullet:** No multi-sentence bullets (use sub-bullets instead)
- [ ] **~100-line limit:** Rules ≤110 lines, split if needed
- [ ] **Trailing newline:** File ends with exactly one `\n`
- [ ] **No H1 duplicates:** Only one `#` header per file
- [ ] **Clear scope:** One concept per file, related patterns grouped
